{% comment %}
  sections/home-final-cta.liquid
  Ported from the "Arcane Flame Website Prototype" option-c.html:
    - CSS: lines ~349-359 (.final, .final__bg, .final__art, .final__art--l,
      .final__in, .final h2, .final .lede, .final__cta) plus the
      .final__art-relevant slice of the <=1080px responsive rule
      (line ~392) — see shopify-theme/assets/home-final-cta.css for the
      full colour-substitution notes.
    - Markup: the <section class="final">...</section> block (heading,
      lede, two CTA buttons, two decorative background art images).

  One-section-vs-two decision: built as its own section, separate from
  the footer (see home-footer.liquid), per the task brief's own framing —
  this is a distinct, independently placeable banner (a merchant may want
  to reorder or remove it without touching the global footer underneath
  it), matching how Dawn and most Shopify themes split a "final CTA" /
  "newsletter" style banner from the site-wide footer.

  Heading, lede, both CTAs and both decorative art images are section
  settings so a merchant can edit copy/links or swap/remove the art
  without a theme code deploy. Both art images are optional
  (`{% if %}`-guarded) since the source itself hides them below 1080px
  and they're purely decorative (`aria-hidden="true"`, empty `alt`).

  Judgment call: the source's h2 hard-breaks across two lines ("Got a
  file?<br />Get a price."), same two-tone-free line-balance pattern
  home-craft.liquid's heading hit. Modelled as a `textarea` setting
  (rather than `text`, which can't carry a literal newline) piped through
  `| newline_to_br`, so the merchant can reproduce the exact two-line
  break by leaving the default as-is, edit it to a single line, or add
  their own break — rather than either dropping the break (as
  home-craft.liquid did) or smuggling raw `<br>` markup into a plain text
  field. Flagged here per the brief's "flag judgment calls" instruction.
{% endcomment %}
<section class="final" id="FinalCta-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="final__bg"></div>
  {% if section.settings.art_image_left %}
    <img
      class="final__art final__art--l"
      src="{{ section.settings.art_image_left | image_url: width: 430 }}"
      srcset="{{ section.settings.art_image_left | image_url: width: 215 }} 215w, {{ section.settings.art_image_left | image_url: width: 430 }} 430w"
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      loading="lazy"
      width="{{ section.settings.art_image_left.width }}"
      height="{{ section.settings.art_image_left.height }}"
    />
  {% endif %}
  {% if section.settings.art_image_right %}
    <img
      class="final__art"
      src="{{ section.settings.art_image_right | image_url: width: 430 }}"
      srcset="{{ section.settings.art_image_right | image_url: width: 215 }} 215w, {{ section.settings.art_image_right | image_url: width: 430 }} 430w"
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      loading="lazy"
      width="{{ section.settings.art_image_right.width }}"
      height="{{ section.settings.art_image_right.height }}"
    />
  {% endif %}
  <div class="final__in wrap">
    <h2 class="display reveal">{{ section.settings.heading | newline_to_br }}</h2>
    <div class="lede reveal" data-d="1" style="text-align:center">
      {{ section.settings.lede }}
    </div>
    <div class="final__cta reveal" data-d="2">
      {% if section.settings.primary_cta_text != blank %}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.primary_cta_url }}" class="btn btn--primary">
          {{ section.settings.primary_cta_text }} <span class="arw">→</span>
        </a>
      {% endif %}
      {% if section.settings.secondary_cta_text != blank %}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.secondary_cta_url }}" class="btn btn--ghost">{{ section.settings.secondary_cta_text }}</a>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

